  "body": "Parking in driveway available for open homes.\r\n\r\nOur vendors are serious about selling! Disregard the CV and online estimates - these figures do not reflect their expectations. If you've previously ruled this property out on price, we strongly encourage you to reconsider. Auction now Wednesday 11 November.\r\n\r\nPositioned in one of Mission Bay's most sought after pockets, 33A Marau Crescent is an architect designed home that combines quality construction, thoughtful functionality and a fabulous coastal lifestyle. Enjoyed since new by the current owner, they are ready for retirement living, this is your chance to secure something special.\r\n\r\nPredominantly masonry construction gives the home a sense of permanence and substance, while generous storage throughout ensures everyday living is wonderfully practical. From the moment you arrive, the emphasis on quality is evident with its lovely oak timber floors and fabulous stud height.\r\n\r\nThe heart of the home is its well appointed kitchen, complemented by an adjoining room that makes an exceptional butler's pantry - perfect for storing all the essentials. A generous dining room and lounge with a gas fireplace flows out to a covered patio that offers some views to the harbour, a perfect spot to enjoy a glass of wine or read a book.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, two generous bedrooms each enjoy the luxury of their own ensuites, including the master suite, where lovely harbour views provide a beautiful backdrop to start and finish the day. With sea views enjoyed from the home, the connection to Mission Bay's spectacular coastal setting is never far away.\r\n\r\nFor added flexibility, the separate media room can easily serve as a fourth bedroom or home office. The thoughtful layout includes an entry level bedroom, ideal as guest accommodation, a home office, or a practical retreat for teenagers seeking independence. \r\n\r\nStep outside and you're just a short stroll from the beach, with Mission Bay's fabulous restaurants, cafes and vibrant village atmosphere close at hand.\r\n\r\nArchitectural integrity, quality construction, superb storage, flexible living and a wonderful seaside lifestyle - this is a home designed to be lived in and loved.",
